. ❯ :ps
nothing to hand over yet: run a line, then :ps (or :ps Out-GridView)
. ❯ .[].people[] | select(.age > 30)
{"name":"Cat","age":41}
{"name":"Dan","age":35}
(2 outputs)
. ❯ :ps
[to pwsh] .[].people[] | select(.age > 30)
. ❯ :ps Out-GridView
[to pwsh] .[].people[] | select(.age > 30) | then Out-GridView
. ❯ :push .[]
stage 1: .[]  → 2 outputs (objects)
.[] ❯ .people[] | $_
[{"name":"Cat","age":41},{"name":"Dan","age":35}]
[{"name":"Cat","age":41},{"name":"Dan","age":35}]
[{"name":"Cat","age":41},{"name":"Dan","age":35}]
[{"name":"Cat","age":41},{"name":"Dan","age":35}]
(4 outputs)
.[] ❯ :ps
not handed over: the line uses $_, which only the REPL has. Use $root, or a value
.[] ❯ :load ../../examples/jq/org-chain/query.jq
dropped 1 stage: . is now what the program gives
arguments from case.json: $root = "E5"
loaded org-chain/query.jq: 0 defs, main in 4 stages  → error: cannot iterate over: null
:defs lists them with what each gives
org-chain/query.jq ❯ :arg root E5
$root = "E5"
$root is now this argument, not the document
org-chain/query.jq ❯ :ps
[to pwsh] -f ../../examples/jq/org-chain/query.jq --arg root "E5"
org-chain/query.jq ❯ :wq
[emit] -f ../../examples/jq/org-chain/query.jq --arg root "E5"
